// Loose "remixing" boundary, NOT a Supp. Fig. 4 confined arena and not a
// pure infinite safety fence either -- see the long comment below for why
// both of those were tried and replaced. Sized for this mission's ~10-boat
// swarm (not the real-lake polygon used in sim/, which is specific to
// Lake-of-Constance geo-coordinates).
// Disabled for the torus arena (Supp. Fig. 3 reproduction): a true torus has
// no boundary force at all, and this behavior's max_range=100 inward nudge
// starts 50m inside the wrap edges set up in meta_vehicle.moos's uSimMarineV23
// `wormhole` config -- left enabled, it would keep boats from ever reaching
// those edges, so wraparound would never fire. Re-enable this (and remove
// the wormhole config) to go back to the open/soft-bounded-square arena.
//Behavior = BHV_SoftBoundary
//{
  // General Behavior parameters
  // ---------------------------
//
//  name = soft_boundary
  // Below BHV_VisFlocking's pwt (100), not above it. BHV_SoftBoundary always
  // claims its *full* pwt the moment it's active at all (see
  // BHV_SoftBoundary.cpp: crs_ipf->setPWT(getPriorityWt()) is unconditional
  // -- only the *delta* it asks for is proximity-scaled, not its vote). At
  // pwt=201 (more than double VisFlocking's) it didn't perturb the flock,
  // it silently overrode it outright -- the original bug this whole
  // Behavior block's history is about.
//  pwt = 90
//  updates = VIEW_POINT
//
  // Params specific to this behavior
  // --------------------------------
  // History: pwt=201 + 90m half-width + max_range=85/min_range=70 meant a
  // boat was "in range" within a couple of real seconds of deploying and
  // then, since BHV_SoftBoundary's target heading is tangent-to-the-wall
  // rather than back-to-center, stayed pinned there -- BHV_VisFlocking was
  // being outvoted by the wall the whole run, not by weak a0/b0 dynamics.
  // The fix after that (pwt=90, half-width 20000m i.e. a pure safety fence
  // no boat could reach in a normal run) *did* let a0/b0 differentiate the
  // flock -- but going effectively unbounded traded one problem for
  // another: with nothing to ever bring separated boats back within
  // interaction range, a flock that fragments (which -- unlike on the
  // paper's toroidal arena, where wraparound keeps giving subgroups new
  // chances to re-encounter each other -- happens *permanently* here) just
  // keeps drifting apart for the rest of the run. That's why MaxClusterSize
  // was capped at whatever a typical sub-flock size happens to be (mostly
  // 3, out of 10 boats) regardless of a0/b0, and why OverlapRatio was
  // mostly noise: with inter-boat distances commonly in the tens-to-
  // hundreds of meters, a near-collision became a rare, high-variance
  // event instead of a real measurement of flocking density.
  //
  // This version aims for a middle ground: a real, boat-scale arena (300m
  // across -- roughly 10-25x the ~12-30m mean inter-boat distance seen in
  // the tightest-flocking a0/b0 combos) with a full max_range=100m free
  // interior (BHV_SoftBoundary returns null / zero vote entirely outside
  // that), so cohesive flocking is essentially undisturbed, but a
  // fragmenting/wandering subgroup will actually hit the wall and get
  // nudged back within a run's duration, giving separated subgroups
  // repeated chances to re-encounter each other -- an open-arena
  // approximation of what the paper's torus wraparound provides "for
  // free". It is still not a real Supp. Fig. 4 (confined arena) or Supp.
  // Fig. 3 (torus) reproduction -- both would need a real instantaneous
  // edge-reflection/wraparound behavior instead of this continuous soft
  // nudge -- but it's a large step closer than either previous extreme.
//  max_range = 100.0
//  min_range = 30.0
//  peak_width = 5.0  //in deg! (legacy, no longer used by the course curve)
  // Course-preference curve exponent: 1 = linear (old, snappy), 2 = quadratic
  // (soft - the boat is drawn gently toward the escape heading), higher = softer.
//  curve_power = 1.0
//  polygon = pts={-150,-150:150,-150:150,150:-150,150}
  //min_speed = 2.0
  //lookahead_dist = 5.0
//}

